WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.984
Welcome back. How do you get your entire team rowing in the same direction,

00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:07.500
on the same rhythm,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.500
especially when everything feels like a priority?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.920
The 90-Day Way is not just a personal tool.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.500
It's a powerful framework for team alignment.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.517
And there's a science to this.

00:00:19.517 --> 00:00:22.542
Researchers have found that sports teams with

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:25.500
high levels of psychological predictability,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:31.500
what we can think of as neurological alignment, simply perform better.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.500
For leaders, this means alignment isn't just a strategy. It's a rhythm.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.420
High-performing teams share a mental cadence that

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.500
maps directly to organizational trust and cohesion.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.500
I saw a team completely transform when their manager used this.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.500
Instead of juggling 10 priorities, she brought them together and asked,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.500
what is the one thing we must achieve this quarter to be successful?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.611
They decided on one critical initiative.

00:01:01.611 --> 00:01:05.500
Every week, their check-in started with that goal.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.500
They were more focused and collaborative.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.500
Your play is to introduce this concept in your next team meeting.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Don't try to boil the ocean here.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.922
Use the framework to facilitate a discussion

00:01:18.922 --> 00:01:22.500
and set one shared 90-day goal with your team.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.500
You can introduce the 90-Day Way, and a team member expresses skepticism,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.500
seeing that it just is another corporate initiative.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.500
How do you address their concern and build buy-in?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.500
Your playbook contains a guide called Coaching Through Skepticism,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.500
with talking points to help you navigate that exact moment.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.500
Now that your team has a plan, what happens when they hit an obstacle?

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.767
In our final topic, we'll talk about this,

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:54.500
and we'll cover how to coach through roadblocks.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.500
See you there.
